  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "One rule for the whole past tense",
      "title_pl": "Jedna zasada",
      "body": "You already have the past of być. Every other verb is built the same way, from one rule:\n\n1. Take the infinitive — mieszkać.\n2. Drop the -ć — mieszka-.\n3. Add -ł — mieszkał.\n4. Add the person ending you already know from był.\n\nThat -ł- is the past-tense signature you met in byłem. The endings are exactly the ones you have learned: -em / -am / -eś / -aś, and nothing for he.",
      "body_pl": "Bezokolicznik minus -ć, plus -ł, plus końcówka z był.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Form",
          "Meaning",
          "Used by / for"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "mieszkałem",
            "I lived",
            "man speaking (m)"
          ],
          [
            "mieszkałam",
            "I lived",
            "woman speaking (f)"
          ],
          [
            "mieszkałeś",
            "you lived",
            "to a man (m)"
          ],
          [
            "mieszkałaś",
            "you lived",
            "to a woman (f)"
          ],
          [
            "mieszkał",
            "he lived",
            "on · tata, brat"
          ],
          [
            "mieszkała",
            "she lived",
            "ona · mama, Anna"
          ],
          [
            "mieszkało",
            "it lived",
            "ono · dziecko"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The same rule on every verb",
      "title_pl": "Ta sama zasada",
      "body": "Cover the -ć, write -ł. That is the whole operation. Here is the he-form (on) of every verb in this unit — no ending after the -ł, because he takes no ending at all.\n\nOnce you have the -ł form, the four personal endings (-em, -am, -eś, -aś) hook straight on.",
      "body_pl": "Zakryj -ć, dopisz -ł. Forma on nie ma końcówki.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Infinitive",
          "Drop -ć, add -ł",
          "he ..."
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "mieszkać",
            "mieszka + ł",
            "mieszkał"
          ],
          [
            "czytać",
            "czyta + ł",
            "czytał"
          ],
          [
            "grać",
            "gra + ł",
            "grał"
          ],
          [
            "znać",
            "zna + ł",
            "znał"
          ],
          [
            "kochać",
            "kocha + ł",
            "kochał"
          ],
          [
            "pracować",
            "pracowa + ł",
            "pracował"
          ],
          [
            "kupować",
            "kupowa + ł",
            "kupował"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "pracować, kupować: build from the infinitive",
      "title_pl": "Czasowniki na -ować",
      "body": "These two look like they should be trouble, because their present tense changes shape: pracować → pracuję, pracuje. That -uj- belongs to the present tense only. It never appears in the past.\n\nThe past is built from the infinitive, not from the present. So pracować gives pracowa- → pracował, and kupować gives kupowa- → kupował. They are completely regular — you just have to start from the right word.",
      "body_pl": "Przeszłość budujemy z bezokolicznika, nie z czasu teraźniejszego: pracować → pracował.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I worked in the office. (m)",
          "pl": "Pracowałem w biurze."
        },
        {
          "en": "I bought bread. (m)",
          "pl": "Kupowałem chleb."
        },
        {
          "en": "Mum bought milk.",
          "pl": "Mama kupowała mleko."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Now you can tell a story",
      "title_pl": "Zdania",
      "body": "The subject picks the form, exactly as it did with był / była / było. A masculine noun takes the bare -ł form, a feminine noun takes -a, a neuter noun takes -o.\n\nAdd wczoraj and you are talking about yesterday.",
      "body_pl": "Rzeczownik wybiera formę: tata mieszkał, mama czytała, dziecko mieszkało.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "Yesterday I played in the park. (f)",
          "pl": "Wczoraj grałam w parku."
        },
        {
          "en": "Dad lived in the city.",
          "pl": "Tata mieszkał w mieście."
        },
        {
          "en": "Mum read a book.",
          "pl": "Mama czytała książkę."
        },
        {
          "en": "The child lived at home.",
          "pl": "Dziecko mieszkało w domu."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
